export default {"id":"bassstation-level-13","number":13,"title":"Portamento & Glide Divergence","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Operate the physical Glide Time potentiometer across linear pitch transition times. - Understand the hardware microprocessor's last-note pitch memory during detached playing.","modules":[{"id":"bassstation-m-13-1","code":"13","title":"Portamento & Glide Divergence","blurb":"- Operate the physical Glide Time potentiometer across linear pitch transition times. - Understand the hardware microprocessor's last-note pitch memory during detached playing.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"bassstation-l-o-13","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 13.1 — Portamento Circuitry and Glide Divergence","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Section Learning Outcomes","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Operate the physical <strong>Glide Time</strong> potentiometer across linear pitch transition times.","Understand the hardware microprocessor's last-note pitch memory during detached playing.","Analyze the operational interaction between portamento glide and keyboard <strong>Triggering</strong> modes (<strong>Single</strong>, <strong>Multi</strong>, <strong>Autoglide</strong>).","Program asymmetric analog glide rates between Oscillator 1 and Oscillator 2 using <strong>Glide Divergence</strong> (<code>g-0</code> to <code>g-15</code>)."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-13-1-1","title":"13.1.1: Glide Time Architecture and Pitch Memory","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Portamento (Glide) is a control-voltage slewing circuit that smooths out instantaneous pitch jumps between consecutive musical notes."},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      PORTAMENTO SLEWING BEHAVIOR\n   Note Pitch\n      ▲                       Target Note (C4)\n      │                         ┌───────────────\n      │                        /\n      │                       / ◄── Continuous Analog Slew Rate\n      │                      /      (Governed by Glide Time Pot)\n      │       ──────────────┘\n      │   Start Note (C3)\n      0 ────────────────────────────────────────► Time</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Hardware Potentiometer</strong>:","Fully counter-clockwise (value <code>0</code>) = Instantaneous pitch transition (zero glide).","Rotating clockwise increases glide slew time smoothly from milliseconds up to several seconds.","<strong>Last-Note Memory Buffer</strong>:","The digital scanning engine retains the pitch of the last played key in memory even after the key is physically released.","If a new note is struck after a pause, the pitch will glide from the retained memory pitch of the previous note to the new target note (unless operating in Autoglide mode)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Load Init patch <code>64</code>. Set <strong>Glide Time</strong> to the 12 o'clock position (value ~64).","Play <code>C3</code>, release it, wait 2 seconds, and strike <code>C4</code>.","Observe the pitch slide smoothly upwards across the full octave interval."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-13-1-2","title":"13.1.2: Glide Interaction with Trigger Modes","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The acoustic behavior of portamento is governed by the setting of the <strong>Triggering</strong> switch in the Envelopes section:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    GLIDE BEHAVIOR ACROSS TRIGGER MODES                     │\n├────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Mode       │ Operational Glide Characteristics                             │\n├────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Single     │ Glides on ALL note transitions (both detached and legato).    │\n│            │ Envelopes DO NOT re-trigger on legato notes.                  │\n├────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Multi      │ Glides on ALL note transitions (both detached and legato).    │\n│            │ Envelopes RE-TRIGGER on every note strike.                    │\n├────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Autoglide  │ Glides ONLY during legato (overlapping) note transitions.     │\n│            │ Detached notes jump instantly with ZERO glide.                │\n└────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>The Autoglide Advantage</strong>:","Autoglide allows a keyboardist to play fast, articulate, unglided staccato melodies, while introducing smooth pitch slides on demand simply by holding down one key while striking the next."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Set Triggering to <strong>Autoglide</strong> with Glide Time at 50%.","Play detached staccato notes; confirm instantaneous pitch jumps.","Play two overlapping notes (hold <code>C3</code> while striking <code>G3</code>); confirm the pitch slides smoothly between the notes without re-triggering the envelope attack."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-13-1-3","title":"13.1.3: Glide Divergence","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"In standard synthesizers, both oscillators glide between notes at the exact same slew rate, maintaining static pitch intervals throughout the transition. The Bass Station II's <strong>Glide Divergence</strong> feature introduces asymmetric slew rates between Osc 1 and Osc 2."},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      GLIDE DIVERGENCE TIMING TOPOLOGY\n   Target Pitch (C4)\n     ▲                       /──────────────── (Both Reach Target C4)\n     │                      / ◄── Osc 1 (Fast Slew Rate)\n     │                     /\n     │                    /   /─────────────── (Osc 2 Drifts Slower!)\n     │                   /   / ◄── Osc 2 (Slower Slew Rate: Splayed Detune)\n     │                  /   /\n   Start Pitch (C3) ───┴───┴──────────────────► Time</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Operational Rule</strong>:","When Glide Divergence is enabled, <strong>Oscillator 2 is programmed to glide SLOWER than Oscillator 1</strong>.","As pitch transitions from Note A to Note B, Osc 1 reaches the destination pitch first, while Osc 2 lags behind, creating a dynamic, spreading micro-tonal detuning swell during every glide.","<strong>Parameter Values</strong>:","<strong><code>g-0</code></strong>: Divergence Off (Osc 1 and Osc 2 glide at identical rates). Default.","<strong><code>g-1</code> to <code>g-15</code></strong>: Progressive divergence intensity (higher values increase the lag time of Oscillator 2).","<strong>Activation Gesture</strong>:","Press <strong>Function / Exit</strong>, then <strong>press the Input Gain key TWICE</strong> (the upper <code>C</code> key).","Display indicates <code>g-0</code> through <code>g-15</code>. Adjust using <strong>Patch/Value ▲ and ▼</strong>.","Setting is saved per-patch into memory."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["On an Init patch, bring up both Osc 1 and Osc 2 (Sawtooth, 8' Range).","Set Glide Time to 50%.","Access the Glide Divergence menu (<code>Function</code> + double-tap upper <code>C</code>); set to <code>g-10</code>. Exit Function.","Play an octave jump (<code>C2</code> to <code>C3</code>); listen to the two oscillators splay apart in pitch during the slide and snap back into pure unison once the target note is reached."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"3. Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Which oscillator glides slower when Glide Divergence is enabled?","[ ] What is the exact multi-press gesture to configure Glide Divergence?"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
